<title>PERU: Peru police say maintenance caused power blast.</title>
<headline>Peru police say maintenance caused power blast.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>An explosion was heard near high-tension electricity towers in a poor Lima suburb on Monday, but police said it was caused by maintenance workers and not by leftist guerrillas as first feared.</p>
<p>The blast was heard soon after 9 a.m. in the capital's populous San Juan de Lurigancho district.</p>
<p>&quot;This was a routine blast,&quot; the local radio station Radio Programas del Peru quoted an anti-explosives police spokesman as saying.</p>
